hand-in-hand  I think visual effects has become much  more part of the world of makeup and  visual effects as well because they know  scanned everything you know CG indicator  markers that we draw on it sort of  become very collaborative as well I know  that Denis likes me to be on set all the  time so what will happen is I'll  generally choose a few actors that I can  work with directly overseeing their look  or doing their makeup day to day so for  instance you know Ryan Jared Leto Robin  Wright but I do find that there are  other directors and certainly other hair  and makeup designers who work very  differently who don't do the set as  often because there's so much prep  involved I find that for Danny that's  not really my style I need to be on set  I need to be where the camera is it was  you know quite involved with Ryan a lot  of out of kit makeup effects and blood  and sweat and and things that I really  needed to be there for their other films  each departments different you might be  having to prep wigs or or you know  makeup we're doing fittings that kind of  thing it just depends on the film but  that one certainly was very hands-on  because Ryan is in every scene of this  film and and I'd be prepping by phone or  at night or on the weekends makeup and  visual effects you know it's always been  I've always worked really traditionally  it's costume hair and makeup I mean the  way Carrie and I work and what do you  think of this we're doing that with  Robin what do you think if we do you  know but with V effects what's  interesting is sometimes were in we're  sort of helping them create a character  so I obviously can't take any credit for  the she's um in the film with Mariette  played by McKenzie and Anna de Armas  that is nothing to do with hair makeup  that's a brilliant visual effect with  some CG indicators on say what we called  new Rita and old Rita or Rachel that was  CG indicators as a character creation  that's purely in the visual effects  world that took 150 people and and John  Nelson and Paul it's it's absolute sheer  brilliance that we just enable a little  bit but other times I think what's  happening  say the pink joy when she's larger than  life's of course they've you know  augmented her size but that's still  fundamentally in camera is a makeup job  the contact lenses are practical  they are sclera lenses the audiences are  very knowledgeable some people still  think that that's all visual effects and  we laugh about it because I think it's a  job the jobs properly done but sometimes  we always have to say well actually that  was in camera and that's very much a  denis villeneuve and Roger Deakins way  of working everything is in camera but  there are other films where they may  actually create the pink character and  I'm you know very quick to say sometimes  the very old techniques I think that we  used were very much part of the film and  and the reflection with Ryan Gosling is  Kay and you know the pink joy was always  in camera it's usually a question of  time there's never enough of it it feels  for me in recent years because we come  on quite late I know they rushed me to  Budapest a few weeks early suddenly we  weren't you know we weren't meant to be  there till the end of June which I think  was an oversight on their part too you  know Denise saying I need you to be here  and you know I'm on another film and  we're all over the place I would say the  challenge to be honest the challenge  really was a lot of the actors were  committed to other projects and I know  Kari couldn't attest to this it would  make me it was frustrating because I  would have would have Robin Wright for  instance who's committed to a television  series in America hugely successful one  and we have her for eight days or 10  days so we know costume makeup hair we  know we have her flying in for 12 hours  one day maybe we get her she leaves  she's coming back to film Jared Leto may  or may not be in the film so I would say  that everyone tried very hard to keep it  as  concise and organized as possible but  for me was quite difficult because I  would have jared leto  confirming he's in the film Alcon saying  yes we've got him we're delighted  everyone's happy it's Jared Leto - next  thing a 15-hour day on the set in  Budapest I get back to the hotel and I'm  having to wait to phone Los Angeles to  speak with Jared and about his contact  lenses and that's another hour - and  then all the semantics all the  organisation that goes into that while  I'm on set 15 hours a day we can't cut  his hair we can't do this you know  there's a lot of restrictions placed on  on us and we have to come up with things  that will work within the realm of kind  of possibility and we came up with two  possible looks for him I would say it  was a huge source of anxiety for me I  don't mind telling people that and the  contact lenses were a challenge  absolutely hand-painted based on a  friend of his who had lost his sight and  and you know they're hand-painted and  there are two people literally in the  world I mean what a job I hand paint  contact lenses it's not something you  just look up in the yellow pages so  there's one person available and we had  ten days so it was a lot of favours  involved to get these what other  challenges I would say coming up with  things pretty quickly or not having the  opportunity to meet someone Dave  Bautista actually was a huge challenge  because it was contingent maybe six  months before Denis rang me up and he  said do you think you can make this guy  look older now I'd worked with Dave  Bautista briefly on a Bond film and he's  one of the greatest nicest people ever  and I knew Dave really wanted the film  and I wanted to help him as well but  they were concerned that he they'd only  seen him in guardians of the galaxy and  inspector and could he look older which  I knew he could so I I called colleagues  of mine in Atlanta where they were  filming guardians of the galaxy  maybe six months before filming and they  did a makeup test - my specification and  it worked and we put photos side-by-side  Alcon signed off on it  Dave subsequently was hired and I'm very  happy about that because it could have  gone another route and he's terrific in  the film and it's a very traditional  aging with latex and it was a you know  not a simple makeup but it was really an  old-school technique that I knew would  work in Denis was very happy with it and  to have Dave on the film was such a  bonus for everybody  [Music]  [Music]
 

